                <pb facs="0308" n="196" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg196"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/3626: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1919-01-11T23:06:00+08:00"
                            notBefore="1919-01-10T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received January 11, 1919, 11:06
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Following from [Harris at] Omsk.</p>
                <p>“14. 10th. General Gaida informed me
                    today that he has resigned his command of the Czech troops and joined the
                    Siberian Army as Lieutenant General. He, together with General Pepelyaev, will have charge of the
                    operations on the western front. The plan is to concentrate troops in the
                    direction of Viake [<hi rendition="#italic">Viatka?</hi>] and Vologda in an
                    attempt to reach Moscow by spring. Harris.[”]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Reinsch</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
